    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c621bbe_70c0ae75",
        "filename": "rust/builder.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 3815749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T15:08:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After reading https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/command-line-arguments.html#--emit-specifies-the-types-of-output-files-to-generate and doing some local testing, it seems that the `-Zno_codgen` does that do anything useful. I removed it. I still think we should have should have seperate `clippy` and `clippJson` rules. Since the `clippy` will be added as an implict dependancy on the crate and `clippJson` will not. Also when we specify `--error-format\u003djson` there is no human readable format printed out, meaning if that clippy rule fails, ninja just complains about a node failing without giving the user any context of what failed.",
      "parentUuid": "777eabaf_f2ae835c",
      "revId": "d0e2eb1e5e3e66035cc506f14867a2a295dcc594",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
